  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Neelam Sharma vs S K Sharma And Anr on 27 April, 2024 In The Court Of Sh. Sushil Kumar, Additional Sessions Judge-04, North District, Rohini Courts, Delhi. Cnr No. Dlnt01-009163-2022 Criminal Appeal No. 161/2022 Ps Prashant Vihar Neelam Sharma D/o Sh. V. D. Sharma, R/o C-6/91, Sector-15, Rohini, Delhi-110089. .....Appellant Vs. 1. S K Sharma S/o Late Sh. Chavi Nath Sharma, R/o: G-345, Gali No.17, West Karawal Nagar, Delhi. 2. State Through App, Department of Prosecution, North-District, Rohini Courtgs, Delhi. .....Respondent Date of institution of appeal : 11.10.2022 Date on which judgment pronounced : 27.04.2024 Judgment 1. Vide this judgment, this Court shall dispose of the present appeal filed by appellant Neelam Sharma, under section 372 Cr.P.C. 1973, against judgment of acquittal dated 24.05.2022 (hereinafter referred to as impugned judgment) passed by the Court of Ld. MM-01, North- District, Rohini Courts, Delhi (hereinafter referred to as Ld. Trial Court) in case bearing FIR No.100/2007, PS Prashant Vihar, U/s. 406/498A/34 Neelam Sharma Vs. S K Sharma & Anr. IPC in case titled as 'State Vs. Anurag Sharma' wherein prayer for setting-aside the impugned judgment of acquittal dated 24.05.2022 has been made.",
    "facts": "(iii) Because the Ld. Trial Court failed to acknowledge that since the very beginning of the marriage, the appellant/aggrieved was harassed, humiliated and tortured by her husband, Respondent No.1, by her mother-in-law and brother-in-law. (v) That the Ld. Trial Court failed to acknowledge that in the light of the appellant's father having refused to pay back the said loan, the taunts and harassment by the husband, respondent no.1, her mother-in-law and brother-in-law increased many folds and they resorted to harassing, humiliating and beating the appellant on one pretext or the other and made the life of the appellant a living hell. Neelam Sharma vs S K Sharma And Anr on 27 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61024999/ 2 (vi) That the Ld. Trial Court has failed to appreciate that during the appellant's pregnancy, her in-laws instead of being happy and blessing her, continued to beat her and taunt her. That respondent no.1 and his wife, who were unhappy about the birth of a female child, neglected the health of the mother and the newborn girl Neelam Sharma Vs. S K Sharma & Anr. child and continued to mete out horrible treatment of the appellant. That within one day of the delivery of the child, respondent no.1 and his wife, without providing any medical and post-delivery care, ordered that the appellant to continue with her daily chores. The appellant, despite being in a sensitive in a sensitive condition, performed all the households chores for the next eight days before her body succumbed, while the in-laws continue to torment her. Thus, she took the newborn baby daughter and fled to her maternal house in order to preserve both their lives.",
    "arguments": "2. Being aggrieved by the impugned Judgment and Order on Sentence, the appellant has moved the present appeal on the following grounds :- (i) That the judgment of acquittal dated 24.05.2022 is erroneous, bad in law and wrong on the facts and is liable to be set-aside (ii) Because the Ld. Trial Court has failed to appreciate that the prosecution has proved its case beyond reasonable doubt. On the other hand, Ld. Counsel for respondent no.1 as well as Ld. Additional PP for State/ Respondent no.2 have strongly opposed the contentions made by Ld. Counsel for appellant and submits that the impugned order has been passed by Ld. Trial Court after considering the testimonies of Prosecution Witnesses and that the same has not been passed arbitrarily. Both of them have opposed the present appeal vehemently and they have prayed that the present appeal may kindly be dismissed."
  },
